{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1140125-holding-actions-and-tied-contested-actions","id":1140125,"title":"Holding actions and tied contested actions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-14T03:04:39-07:00","id":1140125,"title":"Holding actions and tied contested actions","content":"Are there any rules for holding actions or delaying your turn? Say a player want to have his character aim his gun at a door so he can shoot the first person (or thing) that comes through it. All I can find is that events still have to happen in initiative order, which means a whole army of enemies could pile through the door before the character can fire his gun. Am I missing something, or do such rules not exist in CoD?<br /> <br /> Also, what happens in a contested roll if both sides get the same number of successes? Do you roll just again and keep rolling until one person wins? What happens if both sides get 0 successes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T03:24:37-07:00","id":1140126,"title":"","content":"Holding action begins at the marker of the character's initiative (IE, preparing to shot something as you get your bearings and decide on that action); which is impossible to do if the character's initiative is too low to realize the veritable army is pouring thru.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> Subject A has init 12;<br /> Subject B has init 9;<br /> Subject C has init 3;<br /> <br /> If subject A was the one to aim, and B and C would be the ones thru the door in that order, A would be able to shot B.<br /> If subject B's planned action (IE, before he actually can take his turn) is the same (shot the first thing that comes out of the door) subject A would be able to move thru it first because B wasn't ready then. C would be shot.<br /> When subject C tries this, both A and B can move before C has the wherewithal to shot them under said conditions.<br /> <br /> Regarding contested actions? I have them roll again until they're untied. Caveat: In something like a say, a grapple, I have the round continue, with neither getting the upper hand as they keep struggling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T07:45:38-07:00","id":1140163,"title":"","content":"I think in a tie officially the defender wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}